PART A: DATASET PREPARATION AND IMAGE PREPROCESSING
Perform the following tasks:
•	Load an image dataset such as the MNIST handwritten digit dataset.
•	Explore the dataset and examine sample images.
•	Check the number of images and image dimensions.
•	Display sample images from the dataset.
•	Normalize the pixel values to the range [-1, 1].
•	Reshape the images into the required input format.
•	Prepare the dataset for batch-wise training.
•	Create a data pipeline using appropriate TensorFlow/Keras utilities.


PART B: IMPLEMENTING THE GENERATOR
Perform the following tasks:
•	Define a random noise vector as the input to the Generator.
•	Create the Generator using appropriate neural network layers.
•	Use Dense and convolutional/transposed convolutional layers to generate images.
•	Apply appropriate activation functions.
•	Generate an image from a random noise vector.
•	Display the generated image before GAN training.
•	Display the Generator model architecture and summary. 


PART C: IMPLEMENTING THE DISCRIMINATOR AND GAN MODEL
Perform the following tasks:
•	Create a Discriminator network to classify images as real or generated.
•	Add convolutional layers to extract image features.
•	Add appropriate activation functions.
•	Add a final output layer for binary classification.
•	Compile the Discriminator using:
o	Appropriate optimizer
o	Binary cross-entropy loss
•	Combine the Generator and Discriminator to form the GAN.
•	Display the Generator and Discriminator model summaries. 


PART D: GAN TRAINING AND SYNTHETIC IMAGE GENERATION
Perform the following tasks:
•	Initialize the Generator with random noise. 
•	Train the Discriminator using: 
o	Real images from the dataset. 
o	Synthetic images generated by the Generator. 
•	Train the Generator through the combined GAN model. 
•	Record: 
o	Generator loss 
o	Discriminator loss 
•	Repeat the training process for the specified number of epochs. 
•	Generate synthetic images at regular training intervals. 
•	Visualize generated images at different stages of training. 
•	Compare the generated images with real images. 
•	Analyze the quality and diversity of the generated images. 
•	Save the final generated images. 

